␀Configure the PCIE Mode and Width. The link width can be X1, X2 or X4.
The root complex modes are PCIE_X1,PCIE_X2, and PCIE_X4, while the EP modes
are PCIE_X1_EP,PCIE_X2_EP, and PCIE_X4_EP. The EP modes are only valid for
PCIe Port 0.  Note that PCIE port 0 and 1 share the same GSERP0, which is 4 lanes.
This means that if PCIE port 0 is X4, then PCIE port 1 should be set to INACTIVE
or DISABLED, which will cause the port initialization to be skipped for this port.
PCIe port 0 and 1 can be set to share, with a combination of X1 and X2 port widths.
 
PCIE_X1
PCIE_X2
PCIE_X4
PCIE_X1_EP (only PEM0)
PCIE_X2_EP (only PEM0)
PCIE_X4_EP (only PEM0)
DISABLED
INACTIVE
Parameters:
    PORT#: for specified port.
