␀Set the PORTM-MODE for the specified port. The format of the key is:
PORTM-MODE.P#
CNF10KA-specific portm restrictions:
    Ports 8-11 and Ports 16-19 do not support mixing JESD and Ethernet modes
    Ports 8-11 and Ports 12-15 cannot both support JESD modes
Parameters:
    P#: Parameter can be different for each port. See supported modes
        for specified port.
␀Sets the PORTM MAC to GSERM SERDES lane mapping.
Each nibble (4 bits) represents a MAC lane, with the right most nibble
representing the lowest MAC lane. The nibble value represents
the GSERM SERDES lane connected to that MAC lane.
The number of lanes in the GSERM determine the number of nibbles required
Examples for 4 lane GSERM connected to MAC lanes 0, 1, 2 and 3
    0x3210: MAC_L3 -> SER_L3, MAC_L2 -> SER_L2, MAC_L1 -> SER_L1, MAC_L0 -> SER_L0
    0x0123: MAC_L3 -> SER_L0, MAC_L2 -> SER_L1, MAC_L1 -> SER_L2, MAC_L0 -> SER_L3
Examples for 2 lane GSERM connected to MAC lanes 0 and 1:
    0x01: MAC_L1 -> SER_L0, MAC_L0 -> SER_L1
    0x10: MAC_L1 -> SER_L1, MAC_L0 -> SER_L0
Default value of -1 assigns the GSERM SERDES lanes to MAC lanes in order.
See supported portm mode table for more details on the default MAC to SERDES lane mapping.
NOTE: This setting does NOT apply to cn10kas because this chip only supports 1 MAC to GSERM SERDES lane mapping
The format of the key is:
PORTM-MAC-TO-SERDES-MAP.GSER#
Parameters:
    GSER#: Parameter can be different for each GSERM. Optional
