system resets. Must be a multiple of 16MB. Min is 0. Max is 64MB.
␀Speed grade to use for DRAM in MT/s. Hardware may adjust this value
slightly to improve DRAM stability, so scope measurements may not
exactly match the frequency with MT/s. The supported speed
grades are:
    3200 MT/s
    3600 MT/s
    4000 MT/s
    4400 MT/s
    4800 MT/s
    5200 MT/s
    5600 MT/s
␀DDR Hard Post Package Repair When Due Enable
enable or disable hPPR when due
hPPR when due take place if ECS data is collected and present in flash storage
if this option enabled, hPPR On Demand do not take place
    0: Disabled (default)
    1: Enabled
␀DDR ECS Statistics Enable
enable Error Check and Scrub (ECS) data statistics collection
ECS data from flash storage use for PPR
    0: Disabled
    1: Enabled (default)
    2: Erase data (disruptive option)
␀DDR HPPR Disable Repairing Step
proceed with hPPR but skip actual repairing step
    1: Disabled repair rows(default)
    0: Enabled repair
␀DDR ECS EpRC Threshold
If some row is too weak and the number of Errors per Row Counter
crosses this threshold driver updates flash storage with a weak
row id and the next reboot will execute hPPR for updated data.
    128: (default)
    255: Max
